## Choose a service shape

A web service accepts requests. A worker consumes background tasks. A scheduled job runs at defined times. Name the role before selecting the resources.

| Shape | Input | Readiness evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Web service | HTTP requests | A healthy application response |
| Worker | Queue messages | A connected consumer and successful work |
| Scheduled job | A schedule | A completed run with a recorded result |

## Configure before release

Set the start command, environment and resource bindings deliberately. Keep secret values out of source control. Verify the application using the same configuration shape it will use when published.

## Observe behavior

Logs describe individual events. Metrics describe behavior over time. Use both to understand whether a deployment is healthy, and keep the active release identifier attached to observations.

## Publish a known version

Read [deployments and rollback](/docs/deployments) before promoting the first production release.
